{% extends "shell.njk" %}{% block body %}<h1>Privacy</h1><p>FinOps LLM collects information you choose to send by email or through booking flows, plus basic site analytics.</p><p>After you consent via our cookie banner, we use Google Analytics 4 to collect anonymized page-view data (page URL, referrer, approximate location, browser, device type; IP addresses are anonymized by GA4), and <a href="https://clarity.microsoft.com/" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Microsoft Clarity</a> to understand how visitors use this site through behavioral metrics, heatmaps, and session replay. Clarity sets cookies and captures usage data (such as clicks, scrolling, and pages viewed); by default it masks sensitive content such as form inputs. This data is processed by Microsoft in accordance with the <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Microsoft Privacy Statement</a>. Neither analytics tool loads until you accept - decline, or clear the consent cookie, to opt out. You can also use your browser's "Do Not Track" / global privacy control settings or block cookies.</p><p>For audit work, the default scope is read-only billing and usage metadata. Prompt and output content is not required for baseline attribution and is only reviewed with explicit approval for a specific optimization.</p><p>To request access, correction, export, or deletion, email <a href="mailto:hello@finopsllm.com">hello@finopsllm.com</a>.</p><h2>What we collect and why</h2><ul><li><strong>Information you send us</strong> — your email address and whatever you put in the message when you contact us or book a call. Used to reply and to run the engagement; nothing else.</li><li><strong>Site analytics</strong> — the anonymized page-view and usage data described above, collected only after you accept the cookie banner. Used to understand which pages are read.</li><li><strong>Engagement data</strong> — for customers, the billing and usage metadata needed for the audit, under the terms of the separate written agreement that governs it.</li></ul><h2>How long we keep it</h2><p>Contact emails are retained while the conversation is active and for a reasonable period afterwards for business records. Analytics data follows the retention settings of the providers named above. Customer engagement data is retained for the term set in the engagement agreement and deleted on request at the end of it.</p><h2>Who else sees it</h2><p>We do not sell personal data and we do not share it for advertising. The analytics processors named above receive site usage data; email is handled by our email provider. Customer engagement data is not shared with third parties without written instruction, except where a law requires disclosure.</p><h2>Your rights</h2><p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, export, restrict, or delete the personal data we hold about you, and to withdraw consent for analytics at any time by declining the banner or clearing the consent cookie. Requests go to the address below and are answered within a month.</p><p>This site is operated from the European Union and is not directed at children. If this policy changes materially, the updated version is published here.</p><p><a href="/">Back to FinOps LLM</a></p>{% endblock %}
